-- title:
--   Local obstructions at 5 and generators of $E(\mathbb{Q})/2E(\mathbb{Q})$
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be the elliptic curve $y^2=x^3-25x$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, with point at infinity $O$.
--
--   1. **Local facts at $5$.** For $c=\pm2$, $5\mid a^2-cb^2$ forces $5\mid a$ and $5\mid b$. Hence the equations
--   $$
--   r^2-2s^2=5,\qquad r^2+2s^2=5,\qquad r^2-10s^2=5
--   $$
--      have no rational solutions.
--   2. **Constraint on the second coordinate.** If $\mathrm{cl}(\alpha_0(P))=1$, then $\mathrm{cl}(\alpha_5(P))$ is the class of $1$ or of $5$.
--   3. **Special points.** $T_0=(0,0)$, $T_5=(5,0)$, $G=(25/4,75/8)$, with $\alpha_0(T_0)\sim-1$, $\alpha_0(T_5)\sim5$, $\alpha_0(G)\sim1$, $\alpha_5(G)\sim5$ modulo squares.
--   4. **Covering $E(\mathbb{Q})$ modulo $2$.** Every point can be written as
--   $$
--   P=S+\varepsilon G+2Q,\qquad S\in\{O,T_0,T_5,T_0+T_5\},\ \varepsilon\in\{0,1\} .
--   $$
--
--   So $E(\mathbb{Q})/2E(\mathbb{Q})$ is generated by $T_0$, $T_5$ and $G$. This bounds the rank of the congruent-number curve for $5$ by one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/SingleFold/LocalDescent.lean

